<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Jambughoda State</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Jambughoda</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small forest state of eastern Gujarat, also called Narukot, whose woods are now a wildlife sanctuary.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Jambughoda, earlier known as Narukot, was held by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> family in the forested hills near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champaner">Champaner</a>. The estate emerged around 1600, though its founding is known mainly from local tradition.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The ruler governed hilly country inhabited largely by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhils">Bhils</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naikda">Naikdas</a>. In the British period it was a minor state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rewa-kantha-agency">Rewa Kantha Agency</a>. Few further details of its rulers are recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Jambughoda was merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bombay-presidency">Bombay Province</a> in 1948 and became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in 1960. Its forests now form the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jambughoda-wildlife-sanctuary">Jambughoda Wildlife Sanctuary</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panchmahal-district">Panchmahal district</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/jambughoda-state.jpg" alt="Jambughoda State" width="320" height="226"><figcaption>Image: Goran tek-en, following request by Nizil Shah · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rewa_Kantha_Agency_with_all_Princely_States_Gujarat_during_British_India_1811-1937_with_labels.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Jambughoda</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Narukot</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=jambughoda-state" aria-label="Jambughoda State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6654 1352 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Jambughoda State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6974 1608L7364 1601M6974 1608L7364 1602M6974 1608L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6974 1608h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6974 1608h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=jambughoda-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
